  "dense_transcript": "You're the only one who can't be a good friend. You're the only one who can't be a good",
  "notes": [
    "tau=0 runs the full permutation + block-energy path with every block kept (theta=-inf); measured max|dlogit| = 1.00e-05 and top-1 agreement 1.0, i.e. the mechanism is isomorphic at the fp32 rounding floor.",
    "Input audio is synthetic and deterministic (4 kinds: tones, chirp, harmonics, AM noise; 5 s at 16 kHz), zero-padded by the feature extractor to the 30 s window, so the encoder always runs the full T=1500 frames (no truncation was needed; 8 GB VRAM is ample). The evaluated clip is 'harmonics' -- the one whose dense greedy transcript is the most diverse of the four, because tone/chirp inputs make whisper emit <|endoftext|> immediately and token agreement would then be trivially 1.0.",
    "<|endoftext|> (50257) is added to whisper's suppress_tokens during the probe so the greedy 24-token comparison is not dominated by repeated end-of-text tokens.",
    "No human reference transcript exists for synthetic audio, so WER is NOT reported: fidelity is measured as dense-vs-gated agreement (encoder rel-L2/cosine, decoder max|dlogit|, top-1, greedy token agreement, first divergence) plus ROUGE-L against the dense transcript. Absolute transcripts of synthetic audio are meaningless.",
    "Greedy decode is a manual KV-cache loop on proj_out with whisper's suppress_tokens applied; no beam search or timestamp rules.",
    "Block energy is the plain L2 energy of the permuted activation, so energy_captured and actual_skip are measured on exactly the quantity the gate thresholds. p1_v2 additionally scales channels by ||W_down[:,i]|| before thresholding.",
    "The per-token gate still executes dense GEMMs inside PyTorch (mask + gather), so the honest encoder wall-clock number is 'no speedup'; the achievable gain is shown by ffn_operator_speedup, which times fc1+fc2 truncated to the kept-lane count in pi-order (union-of-blocks shape) against the dense pair on the same shapes.",
    "alpha = min(1.5, ||a||/||a_keep||) is applied per token; blocks are chosen per token by the calibrated per-layer threshold theta_l (quantile of calibration block energies). theta_l is calibrated in-sample on the evaluated clip so that tau matches the measured skip rate; pi is built from all four clips.",
    "Note the encoder is NOT FFN-bound: the dense FFN (fc1+fc2) is only ~4.2 ms of the 12.3 ms encoder pass, so a perfectly block-sparse FFN caps end-to-end encoder speedup at enc_ms_ceiling_by_tau.",
    "The two deepest encoder layers are mostly dead on this input: 54% / 51% of their blocks (in pi order) have exactly zero energy because ~86% / ~89% of their GELU activations are exactly 0 (pre-permutation all-zero blocks: ~1% / ~3%). So pi turns scattered dead channels into fully dead 32-lane blocks, theta_l collapses to ~0 there, and those layers are skipped for free -- their theta is not a quantile failure but the requested rate being satisfied at zero energy.",
    "Control for the token-agreement column: adding isotropic gaussian noise to the DENSE encoder output at 0.050 relative L2 (comparable to tau=0.2, no FFN skipping at all) already yields token agreement 0.000 (first divergence at 0) and teacher-forced top-1 0.741. Free-running agreement is a step function of any encoder perturbation on this prompt, so token_agree = 0 at every tau is a property of greedy decoding, not of the gate; dec_top1_tf and first_div are the graded fidelity signal."
  ],
